[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424615976","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111096#issuecomment-3424615976","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111096","id":3424615976,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MH34o","user":{"login":"xuhuisheng","id":1118508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTg1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1118508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xuhuisheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T04:24:02Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T04:24:02Z","body":"The BackBufferCopy's rect mode is really strange. The rect mode will clip the whole screen from left, top corner, using half of width and height. It simply ignore x and y position. The BackBufferCopy's width and height still equals screen width and height. So move out of rect range will get a black result.\n\nChanging SCREEN_UV to UV will paint whole `screen_texture`, then we can see there are only a small area on the left top corner. And editor preview viewport sames have offset issue with rect mode.\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/afa318b5-0c0d-4643-b621-3c0b360eb74f\" />\n\nI totally cannot understand what rect mode want to do.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424615976/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424659511","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111096#issuecomment-3424659511","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111096","id":3424659511,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MICg3","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T04:50:10Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T04:50:10Z","body":"I think this is just misunderstanding of the rect mode. The rect is in global space, so it does not move with the Node. Only the region covered by the node will be copied. So the behaviour in the OP is expected. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424659511/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424758669","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111096#issuecomment-3424758669","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111096","id":3424758669,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MIauN","user":{"login":"xuhuisheng","id":1118508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTg1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1118508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xuhuisheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T05:35:50Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T05:35:50Z","body":"In fact, I am curious about the intention of the rect mode. At first glance, I can use the rect mode to obtain the sub viewport of the screen, later I found the rect mode will provide the entire screen with a portion in the upper left corner. So I confused why we need another part of screen area, and we can only use a quater of it. Because of we cannot change its position, only lower right part of rect really used.\n﻿\nNevertheless, viewport mode works well. Althought viewport mode is not default mode.\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424758669/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424789372","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111096#issuecomment-3424789372","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111096","id":3424789372,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MIiN8","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T05:47:38Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T05:47:38Z","body":"The rect mode is for when you only want a portion of the screen. It is a performance optimization. \n\nLike I said, it is in global coordinates. If your camera moves up and to the left, the rest of the default rect will be exposed. Or you can move the x and y position of the rect to be wherever you want it to be. ","author_association":"MEMBER","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424789372/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424851851","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111096#issuecomment-3424851851","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111096","id":3424851851,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MIxeL","user":{"login":"xuhuisheng","id":1118508,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMTg1MDg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1118508?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng","html_url":"https://github.com/xuhuisheng","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/xuhuisheng/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T06:08:41Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T06:08:41Z","body":"@clayjohn \n\nThank you. I find my problem. When I moved `BackBufferCopy` in editor's 2D scene using cursor. The property I changed is position of `Node2D`, not `rect.xy` of `BackBufferCopy`. By its behavior, I misunderstand that I cannot move `BackBufferCopy`.\n\nAfter I `rect.xy` manually, I can see the `BackBufferCopy` moved. But editor preview seems not sync with game view.\n\n<img width=\"1920\" height=\"1080\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/f2e71a91-a7c9-4942-b6a2-e750944ad803\" />\n\n ","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3424851851/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3427096925","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/111096#issuecomment-3427096925","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/111096","id":3427096925,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7MRVld","user":{"login":"BluesM18A1","id":36201999,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM2MjAxOTk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/36201999?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluesM18A1","html_url":"https://github.com/BluesM18A1","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluesM18A1/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluesM18A1/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluesM18A1/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluesM18A1/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluesM18A1/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluesM18A1/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluesM18A1/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluesM18A1/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BluesM18A1/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-10-21T14:50:41Z","updated_at":"2025-10-21T14:52:42Z","body":"> I think this is just misunderstanding of the rect mode. The rect is in global space, so it does not move with the Node. Only the region covered by the node will be copied. So the behaviour in the OP is expected.\n\nI understand how it works now. Though I wouldn't 